
# Apollon recovery: the production kernel must not print the DEBUG-kernel
# notice ("trace_printk() being used. Allocating extra memory.") when an
# upstream trace_printk() call site first runs. Recovery has no tracing
# consumer - the decrypt-stall work used dmesg and SysRq only - and with
# FTRACE off trace_printk() compiles away entirely.
# The build asserts this holds, so a defconfig bump that re-enables FTRACE
# fails loudly instead of silently shipping the notice again.
# CONFIG_FTRACE is not set
